<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2801" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antĕ-signānus</span></b> ,
		i, m.
		signum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that is before the standard;</i> hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antesignant (sc. milites),</span>”
				<i>a chosen band of Roman soldiers who fought before the
						standards</i>, <i>and served for their defence</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 1, 43</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 22, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 39</span></i>; Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 553,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a leader</i>, <i>commander</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in acie Pharsalicā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 2, 29</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 147,
		12</span></i>.</div>
